    "lawCode": "Add §605-g, R & SS L",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6598\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\nproviding accidental disability retirement for deputy sheriffs in\nSuffolk county\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation clarifies situations in which a Deputy Sheriff in\nSuffolk County is entitled to accidental disability retirement and the\namount of the disability retirement benefits.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a new Section 605-G to the Retirement and Social\n\nSecurity Law. This new section provides 3/4 accidental disability bene-\nfits to Suffolk County deputy sheriffs who were hired on or after July\n27, 1976, and are injured in the line of duty.\n\nSection 2 provides that the cost of implementing this change to the\nRetirement and Social Security Law shall be borne by Suffolk County.\n\nSection 3 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nDeputy Sheriffs work hard within their communities to ensure the safety\nof all citizens. This legislation recognizes the potential danger that\ntheir job duties entail and will ensure that deputy sheriffs within\nSuffolk are appropriately compensated when they are injured on the job.\n\nCurrent disability benefits for Suffolk County Deputy Sheriffs are two-\nthirds of the final average salary minus worker's compensation.  This\nlegislation would increase the amount Suffolk Deputy Sheriffs would\nreceive, if they are receiving accidental disability retirement, to\nthree quarters of the final average salary minus worker's compensation.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nSTATE AND LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee fiscal note.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
